name: Incognidium Browser Team
context: |
  The Incognidium team builds and tests a web browser engine written in Rust.
  The browser renders HTML/CSS with a custom layout engine, paints with tiny-skia,
  and runs JavaScript via the Boa engine.

  Key test sites: news.ycombinator.com, lite.cnn.com, text.npr.org,
  en.wikipedia.org, craigslist.org, google.com, github.com

  render_to_png binary: cargo run --release --bin render_to_png <url> <output.png>
  Firefox comparison: firefox --headless --screenshot <output.png> --window-size=1024,2000 <url>

  File-based knowledge memory (mirrors npcpy):
    - .knowledge.yaml                   -> hidden knowledge graph with structured facts/concepts/links
    - ~/.claude/projects/-home-caug-incognidium/memory/*.md  -> approved Markdown memories
    - ~/.claude/projects/-home-caug-incognidium/memory/MEMORY.md -> memory index
  Read them at the start of every task and append 1-3 concrete lessons at the end.

  Knowledge helper script: scripts/knowledge.py
  Knowledge manager NPC:  npc_team/knowledge_manager.npc

  The codebase is a Rust workspace at /home/caug/incognidium with crates for
  dom, html, css, style, layout, paint, net, and shell.

forenpc: renderer
model: kimi-k2.6:cloud
provider: ollama
